window.MT2FW_SEARCH_INDEX = [{"title": "Build a mod with an agent", "href": "agents/start.html", "text": " # Build a mod with an agent Use the same public contract and complete examples as a human modder. The current Lua API is **1.0.0**; the framework is **0.1.4** and native C ABI is **1**. The [compatibility page](../compatibility.md) identifies the supported game build. ## Context to give your agent Read this page, the [quickstart](../quickstart.md), [API reference](../reference/index.md) and [machine contract](../public/api/1.0.0/api.json). A generated project includes `AGENTS.md`, `.mt2fw/mt2.lua` and `.mt2fw/api.json` for offline use. Source examples are under `examples/` in the SDK documentation bundle and repository. Use `.md` counterparts of the HTML pages for compact reading, or follow [llms.txt](../public/llms.txt). Discovery by an agent is not automatic; provide the entry file or link explicitly. Documentation exports include a versioned Markdown copy under `versions/1.0.0/`. ## Author and validate ```powershell mt2fw new yourname.hello C:/Mods/yourname.hello --template hello mt2fw check C:/Mods/yourname.hello mt2fw pack C:/Mods/yourname.hello C:/Mods/hello-1.0.0.zip ``` Edit only the generated mod. Keep its namespace and declare capabilities. Register windows once, keep widget calls inside render callbacks, and wait for `world_ready` before world-dependent work. `start` is still preparation. The first Hello template has a `local message` line that can be changed directly. To add a setting, define it with `mt2.config.define` and read it inside your window. Use the complete `examples/config` project and the [function contract](../reference/functions/config-define.md). Lua needs no compiler. ## Rules that prevent damaging mistakes - Preserve exact handle UIDs as strings. World epochs expire. Persist supported building references with world storage and confirmed saves. - Accepted actions are queued. Only confirmed is success. Preserve unknown outcomes and inspect state; never auto-retry a mutation. - Lua reload replaces registrations but does not undo world changes. Content/native changes need restart. - Use public APIs only. Raw addresses, arbitrary process starts and native Lua modules are outside the regular Lua contract. - Keep source/package checks distinct from real game acceptance. A synthetic host can prove syntax and API wiring, not native world effects. ## Verify the result Check the generated manifest, run `check`, pack outside the source folder, and retain output and package hash. Then load the mod in an owned profile, edit the greeting, reload and inspect the visible result. Ask the human for genuinely missing intent, not for routine reversible authoring choices. Framework contributors should also read repository `AGENTS.md` and [contributor build guide](../contributing/build.md). Human newcomer timing and multiplayer bridge acceptance remain separate release gates. "}, {"title": "Compatibility and status", "href": "compatibility.html", "text": " # Compatibility and status This is a public development preview: framework **0.1.4**, Lua API **1.0.0**, native ABI **1**. It supports only Windows x64 with Steam and the exact verified MT2 executable: ```text bbab2dc68babcc644d0a1679548bf1e334b6c52aea669c3f61f6cb9d45c1aaf6 ``` Unsupported game builds leave the adapter and mods disabled and report the cause. A signature match alone never establishes compatibility. The installer preserves unknown loaders and original game archives. The runtime does not resolve internal game functions through the executable's symbol table. The adapter uses addresses and byte checks for the verified build. Symbols have helped with reverse engineering, so removing them makes future adapter work harder. A changed executable, including one with only its symbol table removed, still needs compatibility checks and an adapter update before support is enabled. ## Accepted behavior Retained private-game checks cover independent Lua/native plugins, shared hooks, transactional Lua replacement, callback failure isolation, camera/time controls, native place/move/remove operations, stale handles, two authored GLB packs, persistent building identity and missing-content load rejection. Portable installation, update, ZIP import and removal were checked on a separate game copy, including Unicode profile/world names. The empty-core p95 measured 0.3478 ms over 2048 samples in the retained paused fixture. The baseline includes the measurement probe and diagnostics, so this is not a pure uninstrumented-game benchmark. Candidate hashes remain in the acceptance record. New source/build checks do not retroactively change those historical hashes. ## Current limits - Lua is primary. C# integration is not part of this candidate. - GLB conversion is static scenery; animation and skeletons are unsupported. - Selected objects expose verified public handle/position information, not arbitrary native properties. - Root-world building references can persist; unsupported targets are rejected. - Native plugins are not unloaded during a session. Native memory faults can terminate the game. - Human newcomer timing is pending. Automated onboarding does not establish a human ten-minute claim. - Multiplayer bridge F with two separate Steam accounts is pending. Shared writes and multiplayer compatibility are not advertised. ## Reload and migration Lua script reload stages a replacement and commits registrations at frame end. Failed replacements keep the old instance. Already executed world actions remain. Content and native plugin updates require restart. Stable API changes stay compatible within the documented API major version. Check [generated changes](reference/changes.md), the versioned contract and migration notes before updating. A function signature check cannot establish unchanged behavior by itself. "}, {"title": "Build and contribute", "href": "contributing/build.html", "text": " # Build and contribute Use Windows x64, Visual Studio 2022 Desktop development with C++, CMake 3.24 or newer, Python 3.11 or newer, and Node 22 or newer for documentation. The repository vendors native dependencies, including pinned Lua 5.4.9 source, and needs no multiplayer checkout or installed game to compile and run core/example checks. ```powershell python tools/build.py python -m unittest discover -s tests -p \"test_*.py\" python tools/check_contract.py ``` Builds and detailed logs stay under ignored `build/` and `artifacts/`. `--core-only` omits the Windows adapter. `--skip-tests` is available when the unchanged core scope has already passed and the affected scope is checked separately. ## Build documentation ```powershell npm ci --ignore-scripts python tools/generate_docs.py npm run docs:build npm run docs:test ``` The API contract generates the Lua SDK, public function/event/type pages, schemas and change report. The native ABI page includes the authoritative header declarations. Examples are included from real project files. `--check` reports stale outputs without rewriting them. The documentation build produces `dist/docs/site/`, `dist/docs/offline/` and `dist/docs/markdown/`. Open the offline `index.html` directly. All images, search data and code copying work without a server or CDN. Browser tests use Playwright Chromium; set `CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE` to reuse an installed browser. ## Build portable tools and a local product ```powershell python tools/build_helper.py --bootstrap build/helper-env/Scripts/python.exe tools/package_product.py ``` Build documentation first. The helper embeds the same generated SDK, contract, agent guide and offline documentation. The package builder includes only owned runtime files, SDK/templates, examples and notices. It never installs into the real game or publishes the result. ## Source map `src/core` owns plugin/runtime services. `src/loader` owns bootstrap and forwarding. `adapters/mt2` owns game layouts and exact-build guards; its internal extracted namespace is not public SDK. `third_party` has pinned native sources and original notices. `licenses` records origin and file hashes. Do not distribute original game binaries, archives, private profiles or disassembly. Preserve the original multiplayer project's license and data. Real-game acceptance requires an owned process and separate profile; evidence from documentation checks must not be described as game acceptance. "}, {"title": "Native document UI (experimental)", "href": "experimental/native-document-ui.html", "text": " # Native document UI (experimental) Framework 0.1.4 adds a central app launcher, native game windows and an optional document renderer to the native host JSON interface. These experimental operations are separate from stable Lua API 1.0.0. The C ABI stays at version 1. The [machine contract](../public/api/experimental/native-document-ui.json) defines the accepted fields and limits. Call these operations from a `render` callback with the `ui` capability. The host supplies the calling mod's identity. Never supply another mod's identity. Networking and PNG decoding belong in a worker, not in the render callback. ## Central entry and native windows The in-game bottom-right start menu contains **Mods...** before **Options...**. It opens the same native Mods window as the desktop icon and optional framework F10 shortcut. Mods do not need separate function keys. Call `ui.app` every render callback, including while your app is closed: ```json {\"id\":\"main\",\"title\":\"My mod\"} ``` This registers one app for the calling active mod instance. The selected mod receives an **Open My mod** button. The response `{\"open_requested\":true}` consumes that app's launch request. It is never sent to another mod. A replacement instance registers again; inactive instances cannot launch. Keep the app ID and title stable. Call `ui.native` while open to display an actual game-owned window: ```json { \"id\":\"main\",\"open\":true,\"width\":600,\"height\":400, \"widgets\":[ {\"id\":\"search\",\"type\":\"input\",\"x\":20,\"y\":24,\"width\":400,\"height\":34,\"value\":\"\"}, {\"id\":\"import\",\"type\":\"button\",\"x\":20,\"y\":80,\"width\":180,\"height\":34,\"text\":\"Import card\"} ] } ``` The response contains `ready`, `open`, `clicked` and `values`. Wait if `ready` is false during a mode transition. Store input changes from `values`, process `clicked` once, and stop submitting after the user closes the window. To reopen, wait for the next launcher request. The native close button, window placement, text fields, button activation and Escape handling belong to MT2. Framework management temporarily hides the app window and restores it when closed. The window uses native MT2 blue panel materials. Buttons support style button (primary action), tab, row and quiet. Panels use tone subtle for recessed content and preview for the main reading area. Text supports muted and error tones. These are bounded native styles, not arbitrary resource paths. Layout is fixed for a mod instance; changes to positions, widget types, sizes or IDs require a restart. Change text, values, visibility, disabled and selected states without rebuilding the layout. All widgets stay inside the window. The machine contract lists supported fields and budgets. No filesystem read or layout-file write occurs on unchanged frames. Native images use immutable original PNG files in the mod-owned `cache/ .png` directory. The host checks the filename hash, PNG signature, dimensions and size, then creates a namespaced material. Previews are limited to 1 MiB, 2048 pixels per dimension and 128 unique images per session. Game-owned materials remain loaded for the session. Keep card transfer and image decoding outside render callbacks. The existing document renderer below remains available for developer tools. ## Documents Submit a complete document each frame. Keep document and widget IDs stable. Containers scope their child IDs. The renderer owns the window, styles and balanced ImGui scopes, including error paths. ```json { \"document\": { \"id\": \"browser\", \"title\": \"My card browser\", \"width\": 1120, \"height\": 660, \"content\": { \"type\": \"panel\", \"id\": \"main\", \"children\": [ {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Community cards\", \"tone\": \"heading\"}, {\"type\": \"input\", \"id\": \"search\", \"hint\": \"Search names...\", \"value\": \"\"}, {\"type\": \"button\", \"id\": \"import\", \"text\": \"Import card\", \"primary\": true} ] } } } ``` The result is `{\"clicked\": [\"import\"], \"values\": {\"search\": \"Dragon\"}, \"open\": true}`. `clicked` and `values` contain only changes in this frame. Store input values in the mod. Stop submitting a document when `open` becomes false. Escape closes the focused document. | Widget | Fields | | --- | --- | | `text` | `text`, optional `tone`: `heading`, `muted`, `success`, `error` | | `button` | `id`, `text`, optional `primary`, `selected`, `disabled`, `width` | | `input` | `id`, `value`, `hint`, optional `disabled`; maximum 256 UTF-8 bytes | | `selectable` | `id`, `title`, `subtitle`, optional `selected`, `disabled` | | `image` | `image` cache ID, optional maximum `width`, `height`; aspect ratio preserved | | `panel` | `id`, `children`, optional `height` for a scrollable region | | `columns` | `children`; child `width` fixes a column, zero uses remaining space | | `separator` | No extra fields | | `space` | Optional `height` | Limits: 200 widgets, depth 8, four columns per container, 2048 bytes per widget string and 4096 pixels per widget dimension. Invalid definitions return a host error before rendering begins. Window title and identity are limited to 128 bytes. Document windows initially fit the game viewport and can be resized. ## Images Write an immutable preview file under the calling mod's own `data/ /` directory. Its binary format is the eight bytes `M2RGBA1\\0`, little-endian unsigned 32-bit width and height, then tightly packed RGBA8 pixels. Dimensions must be 1-2048 pixels, with exactly `16 + width * height * 4` bytes. Keep the original PNG separate and unchanged. Call `ui.image.load` with `{\"id\": \" \", \"path\": \"cache/ .rgba\"}`. Paths must be relative to this mod's data directory. Parent traversal, absolute paths and reparse points are rejected. A confirmed result is `{\"id\": \" \", \"ready\": true}`. This first call reads and uploads the bounded file. Repeated calls with the same ID reuse the texture. Use a new content hash when pixels change. Each mod retains up to 16 textures. Least recently used textures are evicted. Inactive owners and textures unused for 1800 render frames are collected on the render thread. Texture upload restores the game's previous OpenGL unpack and texture bindings. Keyboard events captured by a document stay in the framework. Text entry suppresses letter hotkeys while function-key bindings remain available. This is shared framework behavior, so other native mods can reuse it. ## Open apps in the game ![Mods... before Options...](../public/media/mods-menu-entry.png) ![Open Card Vault from Mods](../public/media/mod-apps.png) "}, {"title": "Settings and storage", "href": "guides/config-storage.html", "text": " # Settings and storage Define settings once. The Mods menu shows the schema and saves each mod's values inside its profile. ```lua mt2.config.define(\"greeting\", { type = \"string\", default = \"Hello, MT2!\", label = \"Greeting\" }) mt2.ui.window(\"My greeting\", function() mt2.ui.text(mt2.config.get(\"greeting\")) end) ``` Declare `ui` for this window. Boolean, integer, number and string settings are supported. Numeric schemas can define `min` and `max`; setting a wrong type or an out-of-range value reports an error. ## Keep profile data `mt2.storage.get(key, default)` and `set(key, value)` use the current mod's profile data. Use JSON-compatible values. Each scope has a 1 MiB budget. Arbitrary filesystem APIs, processes and native Lua DLLs are outside the regular Lua contract. ```lua mt2.events.on(\"start\", function() local starts = mt2.storage.get(\"starts\", 0) mt2.storage.set(\"starts\", starts + 1) end) ``` ## Keep world data Use the `\"world\"` scope only while a world is loaded. Data is associated with the exact confirmed game save. A `saved` event means the original save and its framework metadata have been confirmed. ```lua mt2.events.on(\"world_ready\", function() local visits = mt2.storage.get(\"visits\", 0, \"world\") mt2.storage.set(\"visits\", visits + 1, \"world\") end) ``` For root-world buildings, store `mt2.objects.persist(handle)` in world data, then use `mt2.objects.resolve(id)` after loading. The framework validates saved identity before returning a new handle. A deleted or mismatched building is an error, not a reason to create a replacement automatically. See [config](../reference/functions/config-define.md), [storage](../reference/functions/storage-get.md), [types](../reference/types.md) and complete projects under `examples/config` and `examples/storage`. "}, {"title": "Events and input", "href": "guides/events-input.html", "text": " # Events and input Register event subscriptions once. They belong to your mod and are removed when the instance ends or is successfully replaced. ```lua local token = mt2.events.on(\"world_ready\", function(event) mt2.log.info(\"World: \" .. event.name) end) -- Later, if needed: mt2.events.off(token) ``` The `start` event runs during preparation, before game-dependent APIs are available. Use `world_ready` to initialize work that needs a world. `world_leave` invalidates its session handles. A mod enabled into an existing world also receives `world_ready`. ## Bind a shortcut Declare the `input` capability. Bind SDL scancode 66 for F9: ```lua mt2.input.bind(\"show_message\", 66, function(event) mt2.log.info(\"Pressed: \" .. event.name) end) ``` F10 belongs to Mods. Reserved or conflicting shortcuts report their owner. Input events go only to the owning mod, and mod shortcuts are suspended while the Mods menu is open. ## Keep callbacks bounded Lua callbacks have instruction and memory budgets. An unhandled callback error disables its owner with the original cause. Dependency failures are shown for affected dependents. A failed replacement keeps the old instance, but world actions already performed cannot be undone by code reload. Use update events for small scheduled work. Avoid world scans, file operations and repeated registrations on every frame. See [event payloads](../reference/events.md), [input.bind](../reference/functions/input-bind.md) and [ui.window](../reference/functions/ui-window.md). "}, {"title": "Import static scenery", "href": "guides/scenery.html", "text": " # Import static scenery Bring an original static GLB into the native Scenery catalog. Start with the **Scenery Pack** template to learn the package layout, then use **Import GLB** for your own model. ![Two authored models, including a textured model, rendered by the game](../public/media/scenery.png) ## Preview and convert Choose **Import GLB** in the helper. Inspect geometry, materials, scale, orientation, bounds and placement origin. Adjust scale and export a content package into your profile's `mods` folder. Restart the game before using new or changed content. The importer supports static triangle geometry, node transformations, normals, UVs, vertex colors, base colors and embedded PNG/JPEG textures. It reports unsupported animation, skins, morphs, sparse accessors, compression or material extensions. Materials map to the game's diffuse model; metallic/roughness differences are reported. ## Generated files A package contains `mod.json`, `content.json` and namespaced `assets`. The converter writes a native ModelV1 `.vmb`, material and scenery variant, translations and an editable `.vmd`. The native building catalog loads the binary model; renaming a GLB or VMD to VMB does not convert it. Content IDs use the mod namespace, for example `yourname.scenery:pyramid`. Duplicate IDs and competing resource names are reported. Resources are registered additionally, without merging arbitrary game archives. ## Save and load The framework records required content versions and hashes with confirmed saves. A missing required pack is named before loading, while the save remains unchanged. Keep the pack installed for worlds using its objects. ![An authored scenery building restored after a full game restart](../public/media/restored.png) These real captures come from retained game acceptance. Original game artwork in the captures has separate rights. See [content.register](../reference/functions/content-register.md), [content schema](../reference/manifests.md) and the complete `examples/content` project. "}, {"title": "Install with Vortex", "href": "guides/vortex.html", "text": " # Install with Vortex The [MMORPG Tycoon 2 Vortex Extension](https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/2465) installs the framework and its mods through Vortex. Each Vortex profile keeps separate settings, mod data and worlds. ## Requirements - Windows x64 and Vortex 2.8.2 or newer. - The [supported Steam game build](../compatibility.md). - The player runtime ZIP from [Nexus](https://www.nexusmods.com/mmorpgtycoon2/mods/25) or [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/DooDesch-Mods/MMORPGTycoon2-ModFramework/releases). - A staging folder on the same volume as the game. ## Install 1. Close the game. Remove an existing manual framework installation with its original helper. 2. Open **Extensions** in Vortex, drop in the extension ZIP and restart Vortex. 3. Manage **MMORPG Tycoon 2** and select the Steam installation. 4. Import the player runtime ZIP as a mod, enable it and deploy. The developer SDK is a separate GitHub download and stays outside the game folder. 5. Import and enable your mod ZIPs, deploy, then start the game through Steam. **F10** opens Mods. Vortex manages deployment and removal for this installation. Keep the game closed while switching profiles or changing deployment. Original game archives are not replaced. Unknown loaders or modified managed files produce a named conflict. ## Classic scenery The extension also recognizes model-only scenery archives, including the original [More Sceneries - Lite Mode](https://www.nexusmods.com/mmorpgtycoon2/mods/2) download by Cow. Download such packs from their authors; the extension does not bundle them. Supported archives have one named pack folder containing `.vmb` models under `scenery/festival`, `scenery/prop` or `scenery/table`. Import the original ZIP without adding `mod.json`. Conflicting resource names are reported before deployment. Sign in to Steam before the first classic deployment. Models are placed in the selected Vortex profile and Steam account's game-data directory. Restart the game after scenery changes, and keep the packs required by your worlds. Classic packs use native save references without the framework's missing-content metadata. Deployment, profile switching, disable and purge have been checked with the original More Sceneries Lite 1.3 ZIP. The engine loaded one representative model. Interactive catalog placement and saving/reloading a placed classic object remain unverified; see the [acceptance record](https://github.com/DooDesch-Mods/MMORPGTycoon2-ModFramework/blob/main/evidence/vortex-scenery-acceptance.json). Legacy MT2 Mod Manager `manifest.json` merging and replacements for original game archives are not supported. Multiplayer compatibility is not confirmed. ## Remove Close the game, purge deployment and remove the managed packages through Vortex. Profile data and saves remain available. Remove the extension itself after purging, then restart Vortex. For development, keep source projects outside Vortex's managed folders. Check and pack a mod with the helper or CLI, then import that ZIP into Vortex. "}, {"title": "Objects and world actions", "href": "guides/world-actions.html", "text": " # Objects and world actions Read supported objects through handles. A handle's epoch identifies the active world; its UID is an exact string. Do not convert that string to a Lua number or retain a session handle across world changes. ```lua mt2.ui.window(\"World Inspector\", function() if mt2.world.status().loaded and mt2.ui.button(\"Read selection\") then local selected = mt2.objects.selected() if selected then mt2.log.info(\"Selected UID: \" .. selected.handle.uid) end end end) ``` Declare `ui`, `world.read` and `objects.read`. The inspector reads explicitly rather than scanning every frame. Object lists are bounded to 128 results. ## Submit an action World writes need `objects.write` and a `singleplayer` or `shared` manifest class. Shared writes are currently unavailable in multiplayer. Configure an owned, clear buildable position before placing anything. ```lua local pending -- Call from a user-triggered callback in a loaded world: local function place_my_scenery(x, y, z) pending = mt2.actions.place(\"yourname.scenery:pyramid\", x, y, z) end mt2.events.on(\"action_completed\", function(result) if pending and result.id == pending.id then mt2.log.info(result.status) if result.cause and result.cause ~= \"\" then mt2.log.warn(result.cause) end end end) ``` | Status | Meaning | | --- | --- | | `accepted` | Queued for the game thread; no success yet. | | `confirmed` | The native operation and its readback confirmed success. | | `rejected` | No confirmed operation; inspect the cause. | | `unknown` | A native attempt may have occurred; inspect current state before any further action. | Never automatically retry `unknown`, a timed-out action or an unacknowledged mutation. Requests have unique IDs and belong to their mod. Placement uses native terrain height; movement can settle to native ground height. Lua reload preserves already performed world changes. Move and remove use the same status contract. Native object observers report supported original placement/move/removal as `object_changed`; these notifications do not promise every internal property change in the game. See [actions](../reference/functions/actions-place.md), [persistent references](../reference/functions/objects-persist.md) and [compatibility](../compatibility.md). "}, {"title": "Make room for your ideas", "href": "index.html", "text": " Your next idea belongs in the game Make room for your ideas. Build mods for MMORPG Tycoon 2. Start with Lua, extend with C++, or bring your own scenery into the world. Create your first mod ↗ Explore the API → Windows x64 + Steam Inside MMORPG Tycoon 2 Desktop · F10 Real game capture: the native Mods desktop app. View the full capture ↗ 🛟 Need help or found a bug? Get support at support.doodesch.de/modframework . Choose what you want to build. One framework. Three ways in. { } Lua scripts ↗ Add UI, react to world events and reload your code while the game is open. A text editor is enough ++ C++ plugins ↗ Use native entry points through a versioned C ABI and the shared framework services. For native development ◇ GLB scenery ↗ Import static models and register your own scenery in the game's catalog. Bring something you made A small first step Your words. In your world. Start from Hello MT2. Change the greeting, select Reload, and see the new text in the game. Follow the quickstart → main.lua Lua mt2.ui.window ( \"Hello MT2\" , function() mt2.ui.text ( \"I made this.\" ) end) Register the window once. The callback draws its contents. Know your starting point. Made for the supported Windows Steam build. Check compatibility before installing. Multiplayer compatibility is not confirmed. Read the current compatibility notes ↗ "}, {"title": "Create your first mod", "href": "quickstart.html", "text": " # Create your first mod Put a greeting in the game. Change it. Reload it. Use the portable helper and **Hello MT2**. You need the supported Windows Steam game and a text editor. Lua needs no compiler. Download the [developer SDK](https://github.com/DooDesch-Mods/MMORPGTycoon2-ModFramework/releases), or follow the [contributor build guide](contributing/build.md) to build it. ## Install into your profile Download **MT2Framework-SDK** and extract it outside the game folder. Open `mt2fw/MT2FW-Helper.exe` in the SDK. The SDK includes the player runtime under `runtime/`. Select your Steam game and a mod profile, then choose **Install framework**. Keep the helper package outside the game directory so it remains available for removal. Unknown existing loaders are preserved and reported. ![The portable helper with installation and profile controls](public/media/helper-install.png) The capture shows the real helper. The profile gives your mods their own settings and game data. Existing multiplayer test profiles are not moved. Import a save only through the explicit copy action. ## Create Hello MT2 Select **Create a mod**, choose **Hello MT2**, and enter `yourname.hello`. Select your profile's `mods` folder as the parent. The helper creates the manifest, script, editor types and agent guide. ![The helper's mod creation controls](public/media/helper-create.png) ## Open the game Start through Steam. The **Hello MT2** window appears. Load a world to see its name. Open **Mods** on the game's desktop, or press F10. ![The native Mods app, with the selected mod and reload controls](public/media/mods-menu.png) ![The first Lua mod visible in the actual game](public/media/first-mod.png) ## Make it yours Open the generated `main.lua` in your text editor. Replace its first line with: ```lua local message = \"My first MT2 mod!\" ``` Save the file. Keep the rest of the generated script. ## Reload and see the change In **Mods**, select your mod and choose **Reload Lua**. Close Mods with Escape or F10 to see the new greeting without restarting the game. ![A changed greeting after reloading in the same running game](public/media/edited-mod.png) If replacement code has a syntax or activation error, the previous instance stays active. Read the displayed file, line and original cause, fix the script, then reload again. Other mods keep running. Content packages and native DLLs need restart. ## Check and share Choose **Check mod**, then **Pack mod ZIP**. Save the ZIP outside the mod source folder. Another player installs it with **Install mod ZIP**. ```powershell mt2fw check C:/Mods/yourname.hello mt2fw pack C:/Mods/yourname.hello C:/Mods/hello-1.0.0.zip ``` Include your own source, assets and license. Generated template code is MIT licensed; retain its notice. Choose a license for your original additions. Continue with [settings and storage](guides/config-storage.md), [API reference](reference/index.md) or [agent instructions](agents/start.md). 🛟 **Need help or found a bug?** Get support at [support.doodesch.de/modframework](https://support.doodesch.de/modframework). "}, {"title": "Capabilities", "href": "reference/capabilities.html", "text": " # Capabilities Capabilities belong in `mod.json`. Local mods cannot declare `objects.write`, `time.write` or `content`. Shared writes remain unavailable until the multiplayer bridge is accepted. ## ui - [`mt2.ui.window`](functions/ui-window.md) - [`mt2.ui.text`](functions/ui-text.md) - [`mt2.ui.button`](functions/ui-button.md) - [`mt2.ui.checkbox`](functions/ui-checkbox.md) - [`mt2.ui.number`](functions/ui-number.md) ## input - [`mt2.input.bind`](functions/input-bind.md) ## world.read - [`mt2.world.status`](functions/world-status.md) - [`mt2.time.get`](functions/time-get.md) ## objects.read - [`mt2.objects.list`](functions/objects-list.md) - [`mt2.objects.get`](functions/objects-get.md) - [`mt2.objects.selected`](functions/objects-selected.md) - [`mt2.objects.persist`](functions/objects-persist.md) - [`mt2.objects.resolve`](functions/objects-resolve.md) ## objects.write - [`mt2.actions.place`](functions/actions-place.md) - [`mt2.actions.move`](functions/actions-move.md) - [`mt2.actions.remove`](functions/actions-remove.md) - [`mt2.actions.status`](functions/actions-status.md) ## camera - [`mt2.camera.get`](functions/camera-get.md) - [`mt2.camera.focus`](functions/camera-focus.md) ## time.write - [`mt2.time.set`](functions/time-set.md) ## content - [`mt2.content.register`](functions/content-register.md) "}, {"title": "API changes", "href": "reference/changes.html", "text": " # API changes Baseline: API 1.0.0. Generated comparison covers names, parameter types/default metadata and return signatures; semantic changes require an explicit migration note. ```json { \"api_version\": \"1.0.0\", \"added\": [], \"removed\": [], \"changed_signatures\": [] } ``` "}, {"title": "Command-line reference", "href": "reference/cli.html", "text": " # Command-line reference The helper opens when no command is given. These options are generated from the same argparse parser used by the CLI. ```text usage: mt2fw [-h] {new,check,pack,doctor,install,uninstall,add} ... positional arguments: {new,check,pack,doctor,install,uninstall,add} options: -h, --help show this help message and exit ``` ## new ```text usage: mt2fw new [-h] [--template {hello,inspector,scenery,native}] id directory positional arguments: id directory options: -h, --help show this help message and exit --template {hello,inspector,scenery,native} ``` ## check ```text usage: mt2fw check [-h] directory positional arguments: directory options: -h, --help show this help message and exit ``` ## pack ```text usage: mt2fw pack [-h] directory output positional arguments: directory output options: -h, --help show this help message and exit ``` ## doctor ```text usage: mt2fw doctor [-h] [--game GAME] [--profile PROFILE] options: -h, --help show this help message and exit --game GAME --profile PROFILE ``` ## install ```text usage: mt2fw install [-h] [--profile PROFILE] package game positional arguments: package game options: -h, --help show this help message and exit --profile PROFILE ``` ## uninstall ```text usage: mt2fw uninstall [-h] game positional arguments: game options: -h, --help show this help message and exit ``` ## add ```text usage: mt2fw add [-h] archive profile positional arguments: archive profile options: -h, --help show this help message and exit ``` `new` creates a complete project. `check` validates it without executing scripts. `pack` writes an archive outside its source. `doctor` reads game/profile diagnostics. Installation commands preserve original game data and require the target game to be closed. "}, {"title": "Events", "href": "reference/events.html", "text": " # Events Subscribe with `mt2.events.on`. Callback errors retain their cause and disable the owner. A failed staged replacement keeps the previous instance. ## start Runs during preparation; game-dependent operations are unavailable. Payload: `table`. Since 1.0.0. ## stop Final callback before registrations are removed. Payload: `table`. Since 1.0.0. ## world_ready A world becomes ready, including activation into an existing world. Payload: `MT2WorldEvent`. Since 1.0.0. ## world_leave The world is leaving; old handles expire. Payload: `MT2WorldEvent`. Since 1.0.0. ## saved The original game save is confirmed and associated metadata is committed. Payload: `MT2SavedEvent`. Since 1.0.0. ## update One game update with delta seconds. Payload: `MT2UpdateEvent`. Since 1.0.0. ## render Draw UI widgets during this render callback. Payload: `table`. Since 1.0.0. ## input Owned hotkey event, suspended while the Mods menu is open. Payload: `MT2InputEvent`. Since 1.0.0. ## object_changed A supported original native placement, move or removal was observed. Payload: `MT2ObjectChangedEvent`. Since 1.0.0. ## action_completed A queued world action has a terminal status; unknown is not success. Payload: `MT2Action`. Since 1.0.0. "}, {"title": "mt2.actions.move", "href": "reference/functions/actions-move.html", "text": " # mt2.actions.move Queue a checked native move. ```lua mt2.actions.move(handle: MT2Handle, x: number, y: number, z: number): MT2Action ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `handle` | `MT2Handle` | `Required` | Current object handle. | | `x` | `number` | `Required` | Target X. | | `y` | `number` | `Required` | Target Y; native settling may adjust ground height. | | `z` | `number` | `Required` | Target Z. | ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2Action - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Queues a world mutation for the game thread; maximum 64 pending requests. World changes survive Lua reload. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** Successful world effects are stored by the game when saved. - **Capabilities:** `objects.write` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - A loaded world, objects.write and singleplayer/shared class are required. - Only confirmed establishes success. Unknown must never be retried automatically. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/actions/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT local pending, result mt2.config.define(\"x\", {type=\"number\", default=0, label=\"Owned buildable X\", min=-100000, max=100000}) mt2.config.define(\"z\", {type=\"number\", default=0, label=\"Owned buildable Z\", min=-100000, max=100000}) mt2.ui.window(\"Placement\", function() mt2.ui.text(\"Choose an owned clear position in settings before placing.\") if mt2.world.status().loaded and mt2.ui.button(\"Queue scenery placement\") then pending = mt2.actions.place(\"mt2:Scenery/circustent\", mt2.config.get(\"x\"), 0, mt2.config.get(\"z\")) result = nil end if result then mt2.ui.text(result.status .. \": \" .. (result.cause or \"\")) end end) mt2.events.on(\"action_completed\", function(value) if pending and value.id == pending.id then result = value if value.status ~= \"confirmed\" then mt2.log.warn(value.cause or value.status) end end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.actions.place", "href": "reference/functions/actions-place.html", "text": " # mt2.actions.place Queue a checked native building placement. ```lua mt2.actions.place(definition: string, x: number, y: number, z: number): MT2Action ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `definition` | `string` | `Required` | Registered mod:id or mt2:Type/Variant. | | `x` | `number` | `Required` | World X. | | `y` | `number` | `Required` | Finite argument; native placement resolves terrain height. | | `z` | `number` | `Required` | World Z. | ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2Action - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Queues a world mutation for the game thread; maximum 64 pending requests. World changes survive Lua reload. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** Successful world effects are stored by the game when saved. - **Capabilities:** `objects.write` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - A loaded world, objects.write and singleplayer/shared class are required. - Only confirmed establishes success. Unknown must never be retried automatically. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/actions/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT local pending, result mt2.config.define(\"x\", {type=\"number\", default=0, label=\"Owned buildable X\", min=-100000, max=100000}) mt2.config.define(\"z\", {type=\"number\", default=0, label=\"Owned buildable Z\", min=-100000, max=100000}) mt2.ui.window(\"Placement\", function() mt2.ui.text(\"Choose an owned clear position in settings before placing.\") if mt2.world.status().loaded and mt2.ui.button(\"Queue scenery placement\") then pending = mt2.actions.place(\"mt2:Scenery/circustent\", mt2.config.get(\"x\"), 0, mt2.config.get(\"z\")) result = nil end if result then mt2.ui.text(result.status .. \": \" .. (result.cause or \"\")) end end) mt2.events.on(\"action_completed\", function(value) if pending and value.id == pending.id then result = value if value.status ~= \"confirmed\" then mt2.log.warn(value.cause or value.status) end end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.actions.remove", "href": "reference/functions/actions-remove.html", "text": " # mt2.actions.remove Queue a checked native removal. ```lua mt2.actions.remove(handle: MT2Handle): MT2Action ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `handle` | `MT2Handle` | `Required` | Current object handle. | ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2Action - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Queues a world mutation for the game thread; maximum 64 pending requests. World changes survive Lua reload. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** Successful world effects are stored by the game when saved. - **Capabilities:** `objects.write` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - A loaded world, objects.write and singleplayer/shared class are required. - Only confirmed establishes success. Unknown must never be retried automatically. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/actions/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT local pending, result mt2.config.define(\"x\", {type=\"number\", default=0, label=\"Owned buildable X\", min=-100000, max=100000}) mt2.config.define(\"z\", {type=\"number\", default=0, label=\"Owned buildable Z\", min=-100000, max=100000}) mt2.ui.window(\"Placement\", function() mt2.ui.text(\"Choose an owned clear position in settings before placing.\") if mt2.world.status().loaded and mt2.ui.button(\"Queue scenery placement\") then pending = mt2.actions.place(\"mt2:Scenery/circustent\", mt2.config.get(\"x\"), 0, mt2.config.get(\"z\")) result = nil end if result then mt2.ui.text(result.status .. \": \" .. (result.cause or \"\")) end end) mt2.events.on(\"action_completed\", function(value) if pending and value.id == pending.id then result = value if value.status ~= \"confirmed\" then mt2.log.warn(value.cause or value.status) end end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.actions.status", "href": "reference/functions/actions-status.html", "text": " # mt2.actions.status Read accepted, confirmed, rejected or unknown status. ```lua mt2.actions.status(id: string): MT2Action ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `id` | `string` | `Required` | Action ID owned by this mod. | ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2Action - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Reads state only. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `objects.write` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - An unknown, expired or foreign action ID is rejected. - Only the last 256 completed requests are retained. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/actions/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT local pending, result mt2.config.define(\"x\", {type=\"number\", default=0, label=\"Owned buildable X\", min=-100000, max=100000}) mt2.config.define(\"z\", {type=\"number\", default=0, label=\"Owned buildable Z\", min=-100000, max=100000}) mt2.ui.window(\"Placement\", function() mt2.ui.text(\"Choose an owned clear position in settings before placing.\") if mt2.world.status().loaded and mt2.ui.button(\"Queue scenery placement\") then pending = mt2.actions.place(\"mt2:Scenery/circustent\", mt2.config.get(\"x\"), 0, mt2.config.get(\"z\")) result = nil end if result then mt2.ui.text(result.status .. \": \" .. (result.cause or \"\")) end end) mt2.events.on(\"action_completed\", function(value) if pending and value.id == pending.id then result = value if value.status ~= \"confirmed\" then mt2.log.warn(value.cause or value.status) end end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.camera.focus", "href": "reference/functions/camera-focus.html", "text": " # mt2.camera.focus Request the native edit camera to focus a position. ```lua mt2.camera.focus(x: number, y: number, z: number, distance: number): MT2Accepted ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `x` | `number` | `Required` | Focus X. | | `y` | `number` | `Required` | Focus height. | | `z` | `number` | `Required` | Focus Z. | | `distance` | `number` | `Required` | Native allowed zoom distance. | ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2Accepted - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Moves the local camera; does not change world objects. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `camera` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Non-finite/out-of-range values, unavailable camera and a native camera script still controlling the view are rejected. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/camera/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.ui.window(\"Camera\", function() if not mt2.world.status().loaded then return end local view = mt2.camera.get() mt2.ui.text(\"Distance: \" .. view.distance) if view.editable and mt2.ui.button(\"Focus here\") then mt2.camera.focus(view.focus_x, view.focus_y, view.focus_z, 100) end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.camera.get", "href": "reference/functions/camera-get.html", "text": " # mt2.camera.get Read camera position, focus and edit state. ```lua mt2.camera.get(): MT2Camera ``` ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2Camera - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Reads state only. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `camera` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. - A required capability or unavailable adapter raises an error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/camera/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.ui.window(\"Camera\", function() if not mt2.world.status().loaded then return end local view = mt2.camera.get() mt2.ui.text(\"Distance: \" .. view.distance) if view.editable and mt2.ui.button(\"Focus here\") then mt2.camera.focus(view.focus_x, view.focus_y, view.focus_z, 100) end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.config.define", "href": "reference/functions/config-define.html", "text": " # mt2.config.define Define a typed setting shown in the Mods menu. ```lua mt2.config.define(key: string, schema: MT2Setting): boolean|string|number ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `key` | `string` | `Required` | Setting key. | | `schema` | `MT2Setting` | `Required` | Typed default, label and optional bounds. | ## Contract - **Returns:** boolean|string|number - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Script preparation or an active callback. - **Effects:** Registers a schema and validates an existing profile value. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** Settings are scoped to mod and profile. - **Capabilities:** None - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/config/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.config.define(\"greeting\", {type=\"string\", default=\"Hello, MT2!\", label=\"Greeting\"}) mt2.ui.window(\"Settings\", function() mt2.ui.text(mt2.config.get(\"greeting\")) if mt2.ui.button(\"Use a new greeting\") then mt2.config.set(\"greeting\", \"I made this.\") end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.config.get", "href": "reference/functions/config-get.html", "text": " # mt2.config.get Read a defined setting. ```lua mt2.config.get(key: string): boolean|string|number ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `key` | `string` | `Required` | Previously defined setting. | ## Contract - **Returns:** boolean|string|number - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Script preparation or an active callback. - **Effects:** Reads state only. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** None - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - An undefined setting is rejected. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/config/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.config.define(\"greeting\", {type=\"string\", default=\"Hello, MT2!\", label=\"Greeting\"}) mt2.ui.window(\"Settings\", function() mt2.ui.text(mt2.config.get(\"greeting\")) if mt2.ui.button(\"Use a new greeting\") then mt2.config.set(\"greeting\", \"I made this.\") end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.config.set", "href": "reference/functions/config-set.html", "text": " # mt2.config.set Validate and save a setting. ```lua mt2.config.set(key: string, value: boolean|string|number): boolean ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `key` | `string` | `Required` | Previously defined setting. | | `value` | `boolean\\|string\\|number` | `Required` | Value matching the declared schema. | ## Contract - **Returns:** boolean - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Script preparation or an active callback. - **Effects:** Writes profile settings after successful activation. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** Scoped to mod and profile. - **Capabilities:** None - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Undefined keys, wrong types and values outside bounds are rejected. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/config/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.config.define(\"greeting\", {type=\"string\", default=\"Hello, MT2!\", label=\"Greeting\"}) mt2.ui.window(\"Settings\", function() mt2.ui.text(mt2.config.get(\"greeting\")) if mt2.ui.button(\"Use a new greeting\") then mt2.config.set(\"greeting\", \"I made this.\") end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.content.register", "href": "reference/functions/content-register.html", "text": " # mt2.content.register Register static scenery resources at startup. ```lua mt2.content.register(definitions: MT2ContentDefinition[]): MT2ContentReceipt ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `definitions` | `MT2ContentDefinition[]` | `Required` | Nonempty mod-namespaced content definitions. | ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2ContentReceipt - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Script preparation/start only, before a world is loaded. - **Effects:** Stages definitions then mounts their assets on activation. Content changes require restart. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** Save metadata records required content package versions and hashes. - **Capabilities:** `content` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Duplicate IDs/resources, foreign namespaces, missing model/material files and late registration are rejected. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/content/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.content.register({{id=\"example.content:pyramid\",name=\"Pyramid\",variant=\"mt2fw_example_content_266054d085dd_pyramid\",model=\"assets/mt2fw/example_content_266054d085dd_pyramid/model.vmb\",material=\"assets/materials/mt2fw_example_content_266054d085dd_pyramid_0.mat\"}}) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.events.off", "href": "reference/functions/events-off.html", "text": " # mt2.events.off Remove your subscription. ```lua mt2.events.off(subscription: integer): nil ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `subscription` | `integer` | `Required` | The token returned by on, input.bind or ui.window. | ## Contract - **Returns:** nil - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Script preparation or an active callback. - **Effects:** Unsubscribes the token if owned by this mod. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** None - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/events/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.events.on(\"world_ready\", function(event) mt2.log.info(\"World ready: \" .. event.name) end) mt2.events.on(\"world_leave\", function(event) mt2.log.info(\"Leaving: \" .. event.name) end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.events.on", "href": "reference/functions/events-on.html", "text": " # mt2.events.on Subscribe to an event. ```lua mt2.events.on(event: MT2EventName, callback: fun(event:MT2EventPayload)): integer ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `event` | `MT2EventName` | `Required` | One supported event name. | | `callback` | `fun(event:MT2EventPayload)` | `Required` | Receives the event payload. | ## Contract - **Returns:** integer - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Script preparation or an active callback. - **Effects:** Registers one mod-owned callback; maximum 2048 subscriptions per mod. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** Subscription IDs are session-local. - **Capabilities:** None - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/events/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.events.on(\"world_ready\", function(event) mt2.log.info(\"World ready: \" .. event.name) end) mt2.events.on(\"world_leave\", function(event) mt2.log.info(\"Leaving: \" .. event.name) end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.input.bind", "href": "reference/functions/input-bind.html", "text": " # mt2.input.bind Bind an owned keyboard shortcut. ```lua mt2.input.bind(name: string, scancode: integer, callback: fun(event:MT2InputEvent)): integer ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `name` | `string` | `Required` | Mod-local shortcut name. | | `scancode` | `integer` | `Required` | SDL scancode, 1..511 excluding F10 (67). | | `callback` | `fun(event:MT2InputEvent)` | `Required` | Called for this mod and binding only. | ## Contract - **Returns:** integer - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Script preparation or an active callback. - **Effects:** Reserves the scancode and registers an input subscription. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `input` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - The input capability is required. - Invalid/reserved scancodes and shortcuts owned by another mod are rejected. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/input/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.input.bind(\"show_message\", 66, function(event) mt2.log.info(\"My F9 shortcut: \" .. event.name) end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.log.debug", "href": "reference/functions/log-debug.html", "text": " # mt2.log.debug Write a mod-labelled debug log entry. ```lua mt2.log.debug(message: any): boolean ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `message` | `any` | `Required` | Converted with tostring. | ## Contract - **Returns:** boolean - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Script preparation or an active callback. - **Effects:** Appends to the bounded structured log. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** None - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/log/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.log.debug(\"Debug detail\") mt2.log.info(\"Mod prepared\") mt2.log.warn(\"Example warning\") mt2.log.error(\"Example error log; logging alone does not disable a mod\") ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.log.error", "href": "reference/functions/log-error.html", "text": " # mt2.log.error Write a mod-labelled error log entry. ```lua mt2.log.error(message: any): boolean ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `message` | `any` | `Required` | Converted with tostring. | ## Contract - **Returns:** boolean - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Script preparation or an active callback. - **Effects:** Appends to the bounded structured log. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** None - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/log/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.log.debug(\"Debug detail\") mt2.log.info(\"Mod prepared\") mt2.log.warn(\"Example warning\") mt2.log.error(\"Example error log; logging alone does not disable a mod\") ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.log.info", "href": "reference/functions/log-info.html", "text": " # mt2.log.info Write a mod-labelled info log entry. ```lua mt2.log.info(message: any): boolean ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `message` | `any` | `Required` | Converted with tostring. | ## Contract - **Returns:** boolean - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Script preparation or an active callback. - **Effects:** Appends to the bounded structured log. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** None - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/log/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.log.debug(\"Debug detail\") mt2.log.info(\"Mod prepared\") mt2.log.warn(\"Example warning\") mt2.log.error(\"Example error log; logging alone does not disable a mod\") ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.log.warn", "href": "reference/functions/log-warn.html", "text": " # mt2.log.warn Write a mod-labelled warn log entry. ```lua mt2.log.warn(message: any): boolean ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `message` | `any` | `Required` | Converted with tostring. | ## Contract - **Returns:** boolean - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Script preparation or an active callback. - **Effects:** Appends to the bounded structured log. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** None - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/log/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.log.debug(\"Debug detail\") mt2.log.info(\"Mod prepared\") mt2.log.warn(\"Example warning\") mt2.log.error(\"Example error log; logging alone does not disable a mod\") ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.objects.get", "href": "reference/functions/objects-get.html", "text": " # mt2.objects.get Read a supported object. ```lua mt2.objects.get(handle: MT2Handle): MT2Object ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `handle` | `MT2Handle` | `Required` | Handle from this active world epoch. | ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2Object - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Reads state only. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `objects.read` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Missing world, wrong thread, expired epoch and deleted/unreadable objects are rejected. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/objects/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.ui.window(\"Selected object\", function() if not mt2.world.status().loaded then return end if mt2.ui.button(\"Read selection\") then local selected = mt2.objects.selected() if selected then mt2.log.info(\"UID: \" .. selected.handle.uid) local ok, id = pcall(mt2.objects.persist, selected.handle) if ok then mt2.storage.set(\"selected_building\", id, \"world\") else mt2.log.warn(\"This selection cannot be persisted: \" .. id) end end end end) mt2.events.on(\"world_ready\", function() local id = mt2.storage.get(\"selected_building\", nil, \"world\") if id then local ok, object = pcall(mt2.objects.resolve, id) if ok then mt2.log.info(\"Restored building: \" .. object.handle.uid) else mt2.log.warn(\"Saved reference unavailable: \" .. object) end end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.objects.list", "href": "reference/functions/objects-list.html", "text": " # mt2.objects.list Read a bounded list of supported props. ```lua mt2.objects.list(limit?: integer): MT2Object[] ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `limit` | `integer` | `100` | Maximum result count, 1..128. | ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2Object[] - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Explicit bounded query; do not poll or scan the complete world each frame. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `objects.read` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. - A required capability or unavailable adapter raises an error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/objects/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.ui.window(\"Selected object\", function() if not mt2.world.status().loaded then return end if mt2.ui.button(\"Read selection\") then local selected = mt2.objects.selected() if selected then mt2.log.info(\"UID: \" .. selected.handle.uid) local ok, id = pcall(mt2.objects.persist, selected.handle) if ok then mt2.storage.set(\"selected_building\", id, \"world\") else mt2.log.warn(\"This selection cannot be persisted: \" .. id) end end end end) mt2.events.on(\"world_ready\", function() local id = mt2.storage.get(\"selected_building\", nil, \"world\") if id then local ok, object = pcall(mt2.objects.resolve, id) if ok then mt2.log.info(\"Restored building: \" .. object.handle.uid) else mt2.log.warn(\"Saved reference unavailable: \" .. object) end end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.objects.persist", "href": "reference/functions/objects-persist.html", "text": " # mt2.objects.persist Create a mod-owned persistent building reference. ```lua mt2.objects.persist(handle: MT2Handle): string ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `handle` | `MT2Handle` | `Required` | A supported root-world building. | ## Contract - **Returns:** string - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Registers a persistent reference, maximum 1024 per world. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** Retained only with a confirmed save; store the returned ID in world storage. - **Capabilities:** `objects.read` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Non-building/dungeon targets, expired handles and the reference budget are rejected. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/objects/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.ui.window(\"Selected object\", function() if not mt2.world.status().loaded then return end if mt2.ui.button(\"Read selection\") then local selected = mt2.objects.selected() if selected then mt2.log.info(\"UID: \" .. selected.handle.uid) local ok, id = pcall(mt2.objects.persist, selected.handle) if ok then mt2.storage.set(\"selected_building\", id, \"world\") else mt2.log.warn(\"This selection cannot be persisted: \" .. id) end end end end) mt2.events.on(\"world_ready\", function() local id = mt2.storage.get(\"selected_building\", nil, \"world\") if id then local ok, object = pcall(mt2.objects.resolve, id) if ok then mt2.log.info(\"Restored building: \" .. object.handle.uid) else mt2.log.warn(\"Saved reference unavailable: \" .. object) end end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.objects.resolve", "href": "reference/functions/objects-resolve.html", "text": " # mt2.objects.resolve Resolve a saved reference to a fresh session handle. ```lua mt2.objects.resolve(id: string): MT2Object ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `id` | `string` | `Required` | A saved persistent reference owned by this mod. | ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2Object - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Reads state only. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** Checks saved region/building identity, type, variant and pose before rebinding. - **Capabilities:** `objects.read` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Missing, removed, mismatched or foreign references are rejected. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/objects/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.ui.window(\"Selected object\", function() if not mt2.world.status().loaded then return end if mt2.ui.button(\"Read selection\") then local selected = mt2.objects.selected() if selected then mt2.log.info(\"UID: \" .. selected.handle.uid) local ok, id = pcall(mt2.objects.persist, selected.handle) if ok then mt2.storage.set(\"selected_building\", id, \"world\") else mt2.log.warn(\"This selection cannot be persisted: \" .. id) end end end end) mt2.events.on(\"world_ready\", function() local id = mt2.storage.get(\"selected_building\", nil, \"world\") if id then local ok, object = pcall(mt2.objects.resolve, id) if ok then mt2.log.info(\"Restored building: \" .. object.handle.uid) else mt2.log.warn(\"Saved reference unavailable: \" .. object) end end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.objects.selected", "href": "reference/functions/objects-selected.html", "text": " # mt2.objects.selected Read the first supported selected object, or nil. ```lua mt2.objects.selected(): MT2Object|nil ``` ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2Object|nil - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Reads state only. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `objects.read` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. - A required capability or unavailable adapter raises an error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/objects/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.ui.window(\"Selected object\", function() if not mt2.world.status().loaded then return end if mt2.ui.button(\"Read selection\") then local selected = mt2.objects.selected() if selected then mt2.log.info(\"UID: \" .. selected.handle.uid) local ok, id = pcall(mt2.objects.persist, selected.handle) if ok then mt2.storage.set(\"selected_building\", id, \"world\") else mt2.log.warn(\"This selection cannot be persisted: \" .. id) end end end end) mt2.events.on(\"world_ready\", function() local id = mt2.storage.get(\"selected_building\", nil, \"world\") if id then local ok, object = pcall(mt2.objects.resolve, id) if ok then mt2.log.info(\"Restored building: \" .. object.handle.uid) else mt2.log.warn(\"Saved reference unavailable: \" .. object) end end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.storage.get", "href": "reference/functions/storage-get.html", "text": " # mt2.storage.get Read mod-owned profile or world data. ```lua mt2.storage.get(key: string, default?: any, scope?: 'profile'|'world'): any ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `key` | `string` | `Required` | Mod-local key. | | `default` | `any` | `nil` | Fallback for a missing key. | | `scope` | `'profile'\\|'world'` | `\"profile\"` | Storage scope. | ## Contract - **Returns:** any - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Preparation/callbacks for profile data; a loaded world for world data. - **Effects:** Reads state only. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** World data restores from the exact confirmed save metadata. - **Capabilities:** None - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/storage/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.events.on(\"start\", function() local starts = mt2.storage.get(\"starts\", 0) mt2.storage.set(\"starts\", starts + 1) end) mt2.events.on(\"world_ready\", function() local visits = mt2.storage.get(\"visits\", 0, \"world\") mt2.storage.set(\"visits\", visits + 1, \"world\") end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.storage.set", "href": "reference/functions/storage-set.html", "text": " # mt2.storage.set Store mod-owned profile or world data. ```lua mt2.storage.set(key: string, value: any, scope?: 'profile'|'world'): boolean ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `key` | `string` | `Required` | Mod-local key. | | `value` | `any` | `Required` | JSON-compatible data. | | `scope` | `'profile'\\|'world'` | `\"profile\"` | Storage scope. | ## Contract - **Returns:** boolean - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Preparation/callbacks for profile data; a loaded world for world data. - **Effects:** Updates mod-owned data; profile data writes after activation, never as an implicit per-frame operation. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** World data is committed only with a confirmed game save. - **Capabilities:** None - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid scopes, cyclic/non-JSON data, missing world and data larger than 1 MiB are rejected. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/storage/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.events.on(\"start\", function() local starts = mt2.storage.get(\"starts\", 0) mt2.storage.set(\"starts\", starts + 1) end) mt2.events.on(\"world_ready\", function() local visits = mt2.storage.get(\"visits\", 0, \"world\") mt2.storage.set(\"visits\", visits + 1, \"world\") end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.time.get", "href": "reference/functions/time-get.html", "text": " # mt2.time.get Read pause, simulation speed and clock. ```lua mt2.time.get(): MT2Clock ``` ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2Clock - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Reads state only. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `world.read` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. - A required capability or unavailable adapter raises an error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/time/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.ui.window(\"Time\", function() if not mt2.world.status().loaded then return end local clock = mt2.time.get() mt2.ui.text(\"Day: \" .. clock.day) if mt2.ui.button(\"Pause\") then mt2.time.set(true, 1) end if mt2.ui.button(\"Resume\") then mt2.time.set(false, 1) end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.time.set", "href": "reference/functions/time-set.html", "text": " # mt2.time.set Set pause and speed, then read them back. ```lua mt2.time.set(paused: boolean, speed?: number): MT2Clock ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `paused` | `boolean` | `Required` | Whether simulation is paused. | | `speed` | `number` | `1` | Native simulation speed. | ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2Clock - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Changes simulation time; local multiplayer class is not allowed. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `time.write` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid speed, unavailable world and shared writes without the multiplayer bridge are rejected. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/time/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.ui.window(\"Time\", function() if not mt2.world.status().loaded then return end local clock = mt2.time.get() mt2.ui.text(\"Day: \" .. clock.day) if mt2.ui.button(\"Pause\") then mt2.time.set(true, 1) end if mt2.ui.button(\"Resume\") then mt2.time.set(false, 1) end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.ui.button", "href": "reference/functions/ui-button.html", "text": " # mt2.ui.button Draw a button; true on the frame it is pressed. ```lua mt2.ui.button(label: string): boolean ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `label` | `string` | `Required` | Button label. | ## Contract - **Returns:** boolean - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Only within ui.window or a render callback. - **Effects:** Draws a widget. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `ui` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. - A required capability or unavailable adapter raises an error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/ui/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT local enabled, amount = true, 5 mt2.ui.window(\"My mod\", function() mt2.ui.text(\"Hello, MT2!\") enabled = mt2.ui.checkbox(\"Enabled\", enabled) amount = mt2.ui.number(\"Amount\", amount, 1, 10) if mt2.ui.button(\"Say hello\") then mt2.log.info(\"Hello from my mod\") end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.ui.checkbox", "href": "reference/functions/ui-checkbox.html", "text": " # mt2.ui.checkbox Draw a checkbox and return its current value. ```lua mt2.ui.checkbox(label: string, value: boolean): boolean ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `label` | `string` | `Required` | Checkbox label. | | `value` | `boolean` | `Required` | Current value. | ## Contract - **Returns:** boolean - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Only within ui.window or a render callback. - **Effects:** Draws a widget; assign the returned value in your mod. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `ui` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. - A required capability or unavailable adapter raises an error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/ui/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT local enabled, amount = true, 5 mt2.ui.window(\"My mod\", function() mt2.ui.text(\"Hello, MT2!\") enabled = mt2.ui.checkbox(\"Enabled\", enabled) amount = mt2.ui.number(\"Amount\", amount, 1, 10) if mt2.ui.button(\"Say hello\") then mt2.log.info(\"Hello from my mod\") end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.ui.number", "href": "reference/functions/ui-number.html", "text": " # mt2.ui.number Draw a numeric slider and return its value. ```lua mt2.ui.number(label: string, value: number, min: number, max: number): number ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `label` | `string` | `Required` | Slider label. | | `value` | `number` | `Required` | Current value. | | `min` | `number` | `Required` | Lower bound. | | `max` | `number` | `Required` | Upper bound. | ## Contract - **Returns:** number - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Only within ui.window or a render callback. - **Effects:** Draws a widget; assign the returned value in your mod. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `ui` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. - A required capability or unavailable adapter raises an error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/ui/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT local enabled, amount = true, 5 mt2.ui.window(\"My mod\", function() mt2.ui.text(\"Hello, MT2!\") enabled = mt2.ui.checkbox(\"Enabled\", enabled) amount = mt2.ui.number(\"Amount\", amount, 1, 10) if mt2.ui.button(\"Say hello\") then mt2.log.info(\"Hello from my mod\") end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.ui.text", "href": "reference/functions/ui-text.html", "text": " # mt2.ui.text Draw text in the current window. ```lua mt2.ui.text(text: any): boolean ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `text` | `any` | `Required` | Converted to text, at most 8192 UTF-8 bytes per widget. | ## Contract - **Returns:** boolean - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Only within ui.window or a render callback. - **Effects:** Draws a widget. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `ui` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. - A required capability or unavailable adapter raises an error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/ui/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT local enabled, amount = true, 5 mt2.ui.window(\"My mod\", function() mt2.ui.text(\"Hello, MT2!\") enabled = mt2.ui.checkbox(\"Enabled\", enabled) amount = mt2.ui.number(\"Amount\", amount, 1, 10) if mt2.ui.button(\"Say hello\") then mt2.log.info(\"Hello from my mod\") end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.ui.window", "href": "reference/functions/ui-window.html", "text": " # mt2.ui.window Register a window once and draw its contents on render. ```lua mt2.ui.window(title: string, draw: fun()): integer ``` ## Parameters | Name | Type | Default | Meaning | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | `title` | `string` | `Required` | Window title, at most 256 UTF-8 bytes. | | `draw` | `fun()` | `Required` | Draw widgets inside this callback. | ## Contract - **Returns:** integer - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Register during script preparation or a callback; draw runs only during render. - **Effects:** Registers a render subscription. Never register a window on every update. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `ui` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. - A required capability or unavailable adapter raises an error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/ui/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT local enabled, amount = true, 5 mt2.ui.window(\"My mod\", function() mt2.ui.text(\"Hello, MT2!\") enabled = mt2.ui.checkbox(\"Enabled\", enabled) amount = mt2.ui.number(\"Amount\", amount, 1, 10) if mt2.ui.button(\"Say hello\") then mt2.log.info(\"Hello from my mod\") end end) ``` "}, {"title": "mt2.world.status", "href": "reference/functions/world-status.html", "text": " # mt2.world.status Read the loaded world name and current epoch. ```lua mt2.world.status(): MT2World ``` ## Contract - **Returns:** MT2World - **Thread:** Framework callbacks; native object/camera/time reads verify the game thread. - **When to call:** Active callbacks. Game-dependent calls reject during script preparation and start. - **Effects:** Reads state only. - **Reload:** Subscriptions owned by the old instance are removed on a successful replacement. - **Persistence:** No implicit persistence. - **Capabilities:** `world.read` - **Since:** 1.0.0 - **Stability:** stable-within-api-1 ## Errors - Invalid arguments raise a Lua error. - A required capability or unavailable adapter raises an error. ## Example This complete example is also available under `examples/world/main.lua` in the source and SDK documentation bundle. Native effects require the real game. ```lua -- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT mt2.events.on(\"world_ready\", function() local world = mt2.world.status() mt2.log.info(world.name .. \" - epoch \" .. world.epoch) end) ``` "}, {"title": "API reference", "href": "reference/index.html", "text": " # API reference Public Lua API **1.0.0**, native ABI **1**, framework **0.1.4**. [Events](events.md) | [Types](types.md) | [Capabilities](capabilities.md) | [Native ABI](native.md) | [Manifests](manifests.md) ## actions - [`mt2.actions.place`](functions/actions-place.md): Queue a checked native building placement. - [`mt2.actions.move`](functions/actions-move.md): Queue a checked native move. - [`mt2.actions.remove`](functions/actions-remove.md): Queue a checked native removal. - [`mt2.actions.status`](functions/actions-status.md): Read accepted, confirmed, rejected or unknown status. ## camera - [`mt2.camera.get`](functions/camera-get.md): Read camera position, focus and edit state. - [`mt2.camera.focus`](functions/camera-focus.md): Request the native edit camera to focus a position. ## config - [`mt2.config.define`](functions/config-define.md): Define a typed setting shown in the Mods menu. - [`mt2.config.get`](functions/config-get.md): Read a defined setting. - [`mt2.config.set`](functions/config-set.md): Validate and save a setting. ## content - [`mt2.content.register`](functions/content-register.md): Register static scenery resources at startup. ## events - [`mt2.events.on`](functions/events-on.md): Subscribe to an event. - [`mt2.events.off`](functions/events-off.md): Remove your subscription. ## input - [`mt2.input.bind`](functions/input-bind.md): Bind an owned keyboard shortcut. ## log - [`mt2.log.debug`](functions/log-debug.md): Write a mod-labelled debug log entry. - [`mt2.log.info`](functions/log-info.md): Write a mod-labelled info log entry. - [`mt2.log.warn`](functions/log-warn.md): Write a mod-labelled warn log entry. - [`mt2.log.error`](functions/log-error.md): Write a mod-labelled error log entry. ## objects - [`mt2.objects.list`](functions/objects-list.md): Read a bounded list of supported props. - [`mt2.objects.get`](functions/objects-get.md): Read a supported object. - [`mt2.objects.selected`](functions/objects-selected.md): Read the first supported selected object, or nil. - [`mt2.objects.persist`](functions/objects-persist.md): Create a mod-owned persistent building reference. - [`mt2.objects.resolve`](functions/objects-resolve.md): Resolve a saved reference to a fresh session handle. ## storage - [`mt2.storage.get`](functions/storage-get.md): Read mod-owned profile or world data. - [`mt2.storage.set`](functions/storage-set.md): Store mod-owned profile or world data. ## time - [`mt2.time.get`](functions/time-get.md): Read pause, simulation speed and clock. - [`mt2.time.set`](functions/time-set.md): Set pause and speed, then read them back. ## ui - [`mt2.ui.window`](functions/ui-window.md): Register a window once and draw its contents on render. - [`mt2.ui.text`](functions/ui-text.md): Draw text in the current window. - [`mt2.ui.button`](functions/ui-button.md): Draw a button; true on the frame it is pressed. - [`mt2.ui.checkbox`](functions/ui-checkbox.md): Draw a checkbox and return its current value. - [`mt2.ui.number`](functions/ui-number.md): Draw a numeric slider and return its value. ## world - [`mt2.world.status`](functions/world-status.md): Read the loaded world name and current epoch. "}, {"title": "Mod and content manifests", "href": "reference/manifests.html", "text": " # Mod and content manifests Every package has one `mod.json` at its root. ```json { \"id\": \"yourname.hello\", \"name\": \"My first mod\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\", \"api_version\": \"1.0.0\", \"type\": \"lua\", \"entry\": \"main.lua\", \"capabilities\": [\"ui\"], \"multiplayer\": \"local\" } ``` Required keys are ID, name, SemVer version, API version, type, entry and capabilities. IDs are lowercase and namespaced. Types are `lua`, `native` or `content`. Entry paths are confined to the package. Optional `dependencies` maps mod IDs to supported exact, `^` or `>=` version requirements. Missing dependencies, duplicate IDs and cycles receive concrete errors. The default multiplayer class is `singleplayer`. `local` is for UI, input and local camera, and cannot request world/content/time writes. `shared` requires matching packages and the future accepted multiplayer bridge; it does not enable shared writes in this candidate. Machine schemas: [mod.schema.json](../public/api/1.0.0/mod.schema.json) and [content.schema.json](../public/api/1.0.0/content.schema.json). They describe structure. `mt2fw check` additionally checks SemVer rules, Windows-confined paths, existing resources and package limits. Custom schema formats are `semver`, `supported-mt2-api` and `mt2-relative-path`; generic validators must register them or use the CLI for semantic validation. Content definitions require `id`, `variant`, `model` and `material`. Resource paths remain inside the package. Use the converter instead of editing binary files by hand. See [capabilities](capabilities.md) and [scenery](../guides/scenery.md). "}, {"title": "Native C ABI", "href": "reference/native.html", "text": " # Native C ABI The supported native boundary is `include/mt2fw/plugin.h`, shown below without a manually duplicated declaration list. No STL objects or exceptions may cross this ABI. Plugins remain loaded until process exit. Host strings are copied during a request. Callback JSON is borrowed until return. The host and PluginInfo strings remain valid through Shutdown. A size query never executes a mutation; request a sufficiently sized buffer once, then perform the call once. ```c #pragma once #include #include #ifdef _WIN32 #define MT2FW_EXPORT __declspec(dllexport) #define MT2FW_CALL __cdecl #else #define MT2FW_EXPORT __attribute__((visibility(\"default\"))) #define MT2FW_CALL #endif #ifdef __cplusplus extern \"C\" { #endif #define MT2FW_ABI_VERSION 1u typedef void (MT2FW_CALL *MT2FW_EventCallback)(void* user, const char* json, size_t length); typedef struct MT2FW_Host { uint32_t size; uint32_t abi_version; void* context; /* UTF-8 JSON. The returned required size includes the terminator. A null output only measures; it never executes a mutation. Call once with a sufficiently sized buffer. */ size_t (MT2FW_CALL *request)(void* context, const char* operation, const char* arguments, char* output, size_t capacity); uint64_t (MT2FW_CALL *subscribe)(void* context, const char* event, MT2FW_EventCallback callback, void* user); void (MT2FW_CALL *unsubscribe)(void* context, uint64_t subscription); } MT2FW_Host; typedef struct MT2FW_PluginInfo { uint32_t size; uint32_t abi_version; /* Borrowed UTF-8 strings; keep them valid until PluginShutdown returns. */ const char* id; const char* version; } MT2FW_PluginInfo; typedef int (MT2FW_CALL *MT2FW_QueryFn)(MT2FW_PluginInfo* info); typedef int (MT2FW_CALL *MT2FW_LoadFn)(const MT2FW_Host* host); typedef void (MT2FW_CALL *MT2FW_ShutdownFn)(void); /* Export MT2FW_PluginQuery, MT2FW_PluginLoad, MT2FW_PluginShutdown with these signatures. Strings passed to the host are copied during the call. Callback JSON is borrowed until return. The host remains valid until Shutdown returns. No exception may cross this boundary. */ #ifdef __cplusplus } #endif ``` ## Host JSON operations Lua wrappers use the following operations. `ui.begin` and `ui.end` are native host operations; Lua authors use `mt2.ui.window`. Events use the ABI subscribe/unsubscribe pointers. - `actions.move` - `actions.place` - `actions.remove` - `actions.status` - `camera.focus` - `camera.get` - `config.define` - `config.get` - `config.set` - `content.register` - `input.bind` - `log` - `objects.get` - `objects.list` - `objects.persist` - `objects.resolve` - `objects.selected` - `storage.get` - `storage.set` - `time.get` - `time.set` - `ui.begin` - `ui.button` - `ui.checkbox` - `ui.end` - `ui.number` - `ui.text` - `world.status` "}, {"title": "Types", "href": "reference/types.html", "text": " # Types Handles carry a world epoch and an exact string UID. Never convert the UID to a floating-point Lua number. ## MT2Handle | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `epoch` | `integer` | | `uid` | `string` | ## MT2Object | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `handle` | `MT2Handle` | | `x` | `number` | | `y` | `number` | | `z` | `number` | | `deleted?` | `boolean` | ## MT2World | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `loaded` | `boolean` | | `name` | `string` | | `epoch` | `integer` | ## MT2Setting | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `type` | `'boolean'\\|'string'\\|'number'\\|'integer'` | | `default` | `boolean\\|string\\|number` | | `label?` | `string` | | `min?` | `number` | | `max?` | `number` | ## MT2Camera | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `x` | `number` | | `y` | `number` | | `z` | `number` | | `focus_x` | `number` | | `focus_y` | `number` | | `focus_z` | `number` | | `distance` | `number` | | `min` | `number` | | `max` | `number` | | `script_weight` | `number` | | `editable` | `boolean` | ## MT2Clock | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `paused` | `boolean` | | `speed` | `number` | | `day` | `integer` | | `seconds` | `integer` | ## MT2Accepted | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `accepted` | `boolean` | ## MT2Action | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `id` | `string` | | `status` | `'accepted'\\|'confirmed'\\|'rejected'\\|'unknown'` | | `cause?` | `string` | | `native_attempted?` | `boolean` | | `object?` | `MT2Object` | ## MT2ContentDefinition | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `id` | `string` | | `name?` | `string` | | `variant` | `string` | | `model` | `string` | | `material` | `string` | ## MT2ContentReceipt | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `staged?` | `integer` | | `registered?` | `integer` | ## MT2WorldEvent | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `epoch` | `integer` | | `name` | `string` | ## MT2SavedEvent | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `epoch` | `integer` | | `name` | `string` | | `save` | `string` | ## MT2UpdateEvent | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `dt` | `number` | | `epoch` | `integer` | ## MT2InputEvent | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `owner` | `string` | | `name` | `string` | | `scancode` | `integer` | ## MT2ObjectChangedEvent | Field | Type | | --- | --- | | `operation` | `'actions.place'\\|'actions.move'\\|'actions.remove'` | | `source` | `'native'` | | `object` | `MT2Object` | "}];
